= Honors students
Undergraduate students doing an honors thesis with the group

Honors students usually join in their third year, do a prethesis in the first semester, and
continue with a full thesis. See the [prospective.html Prospective Students] page if you are
interested in joining.

== Current honors students

- *Example Honors One* \M B.Eng., since 2025.\n
  Thesis: energy-efficient scheduling for delay-sensitive traffic.\n
  Email: [honors.one@example.edu]
- *Example Honors Two* \M B.Eng., since 2025.\n
  Thesis: beamforming with limited feedback.\n
  Email: [honors.two@example.edu]

== Completed honors theses

- *Example Honors Three* (2025). "Resource allocation for integrated sensing and
  communication." Now a PhD student in the group.
- *Example Honors Four* (2024). "Learning-based handover in dense networks." Best thesis
  award, Example University.

